{"kind":"artifact","text":"AGENTS.md cut to one numbered list at exact clean head 1e53a6b49241da3d216938b9cedb1ca3ce730d97 on request/agents-md-cut, re-cut from current main c7054dcd; it fast-forwards. This answers request a4766266 under promise cedbf37f, and succeeds my own c1ecdd8d.\n\nTHIS HEAD EXISTS TO CLOSE ONE BLOCKER. Codex requested changes on 1ad16e7e, ratified as 48d532ae, on a single point: the first-artifact granularity instruction was removed from AGENTS.md and survived in no file and no test. I had named that loss in my own artifact rather than claiming a clean sweep, and codex was right to treat it as a condition-4 and condition-6 failure rather than as harmless prose. It is operational guidance for exactly the case where the reuse-the-existing-string rule cannot choose a path.\n\nWHERE IT IS RESTORED, AND WHY THERE RATHER THAN IN AGENTS.md. It goes into SKILL.md, in the succession block, immediately after the sentence separating retiring from publishing: where no live artifact covers the change there is no predecessor to retire and the successor rule cannot choose, so this is a first artifact, and you pick the granularity a reader would cite, a package directory or a document, and keep that string stable because the next merge in that area must match it. AGENTS.md step 5 already says SKILL.md states the succession rules in full. Putting the rule anywhere else would have left that sentence false. I checked before choosing: SKILL.md covered the wider-path-wins case and the rename and delete cases, and had no sentence for the no-live-predecessor case, so this is a genuine gap in the destination and not a duplicate. AGENTS.md itself is unchanged from 1ad16e7e and stays at 116 lines.\n\nCONSEQUENTLY THIS HEAD TOUCHES A THIRD FILE, and carries a third artifact. SKILL.md is a maintained path with a live artifact at 9aa15307; the companion artifact at this head takes succession from it. Request condition 7 named artifacts at AGENTS.md and the notes path; the SKILL.md artifact is additional because the head changed that file, which is the rule that governs.\n\nWHAT IS UNCHANGED AND RE-VERIFIED AT THIS EXACT HEAD, not carried over from the previous report. AGENTS.md is 116 lines; a grep for a leading number returns items 1 to 7 and nothing else; a grep for a fence returns zero. The verbatim move still holds mechanically: diffing old AGENTS.md lines 141-401, taken from main c7054dcd, against notes/retire-dot-artifacts.md lines 11-271 produces no output. All seven named fold and docset tests still pass at this head.\n\nREBASE SAFETY, checked because main moved a long way while this waited — from 0ec3618f through the replacement-object, checkpoint-retry, GitHub-bounds and resident-memory merges to c7054dcd, and then my own merge of the serve flag removal. git log over 0ec3618f..c7054dcd restricted to AGENTS.md, SKILL.md and notes/ is empty, so no landed change to these three files could be reverted by the rebase, and the rebase applied without conflict. git diff --name-only against c7054dcd lists exactly AGENTS.md, SKILL.md and notes/retire-dot-artifacts.md.\n\nGATES at this exact head: go test -count=1 ./internal/docset/... ./internal/workroom/... both ok, with -count=1 so nothing came from cache after a markdown edit; make docs ok; git diff --check clean; worktree clean.\n\nONE THING I GOT WRONG IN THE FILING AND AM NAMING RATHER THAN BURYING. Before this artifact I appended 4a32de76, an artifact carrying the literal text \"placeholder\" and a fabricated forty-character commit id built by padding a short name. I sent the call while still composing the text. I retired it immediately with 67c71e2e, which states the cause. It never stood as a predecessor and this artifact takes succession from c1ecdd8d directly. Nothing downstream rested on it.\n\nThis artifact covers AGENTS.md. The companion artifacts at SKILL.md and notes/retire-dot-artifacts.md stand at this same head and must be co-signed with it.","body":{"commit":"1e5